formation, gender identity, gender expression, or sexual orientation or preference. In support of the University's mission to be inclusive and diverse, applications from qualified minorities, women, veterans and persons with disabilities are highly encouraged. Montana Tech makes accommodation for any known disability that may interfere with an applicant's ability to compete in the hiring process or an employee's ability to perform the duties of the job. In compliance with the Montana Veteran's Employment Preference Act, Montana Tech provides preference in employment to veterans, disabled veterans, and certain eligible relatives of veterans. To request assistance with the application process, or an accommodation for the interview, please contact Cathy Isakson at 406-496-4380 or email her at cisakson@mtech.edu . Employment Eligibility: All New Employees must be eligible and show employment eligibility verification by the first date of employment at Montana Tech, as legally required (e.g., Form I-9). Montana Tech will require proof of authorization to work in the United States before final hiring. Due to the September 19, 2025 Presidential Proclamation and related guidance from USCIS and the Department of State, Montana Tech may be limited in its ability to offer H-1B sponsorship. At this time, we are unable to sponsor new H-1B visas that require payment of the additional fee introduced by the Proclamation. Why Work at Tech? Help meet the changing needs of society by providing a transformative student experience by helping develop leaders for tomorrow by advancing science, engineering and technology. Benefits Package In addition, Montana Tech offers an attractive benefits package* which includes: Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance with low deductibles and comprehensive coverage. Generous employer contribution toward monthly health care benefits worth $6.08 per hour. 5.9% retirement employer contribution for eligible employees 11 Holidays per year 3 weeks of Annual Leave to start Generous sick leave policy that can be used for sick children, doctor and dentist appointments as well as bereavement. 6 credits of coursework free per year (fees not included) Life and Disability Insurance Reduced tuition for dependents after 4 months of employment for eligible employees Employee Assistance and a Wellness Program Optional Retirement Plan for eligible employees Possible remote work days with supervisor approval and eligible positions. *Benefits are dependent on type of position and terms and conditions of eligibility. Clery Act The Jeanne Clery Act, a consumer protection law, requires all colleges and universities who receive federal funding to share information about crime on campus, efforts to improve campus safety, and inform the public of crime in or around campus. View Montana Tech's Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (PDF) . Copies of the reports may also be obtained at the Dean of Students' Office located in Engineering Hall, Room 101 or by calling 406-496-4198 . Head Golf Coach Butte, MT Temporary Athletics Mid Level Share Job Title : Head Golf Coach Department: Athletics Employment Type: Temporary/Part-Time Location: Butte, MT (Campus-Based) Applications received by November 1, 2026 will be guaranteed full review and consideration.  Applications received after that date may be considered until an adequate applicant pool has been established. Montana Technological University provides a comprehensive benefits package for all eligible positions that includes health, dental and vision insurance, mandatory retirement plan with employer contribution, partial tuition waiver, and a wellness program. Montana Tech Athletics is seeking a Head Golf Coach to lead its men’s and women’s golf programs. The Head Coach will focus primarily on what matters most to the success of the program: coaching, instruction, recruiting, and student-athlete development. Responsibilities include planning and conducting practices, providing individual and team instruction, coaching during competition, recruiting prospective student-athletes, and building a positive and competitive team culture. The Montana Tech Athletic Department will provide support for many of the program’s administrative and operational responsibilities, including eligibility and compliance, travel planning and arrangements, and other team logistics, allowing the Head Coach to focus on coaching and developing student-athletes. We are seeking a candidate with a strong knowledge of golf, the ability to teach and develop players, and a commitment to building positive relationships with student-athletes. Previous coaching or instructional experience is preferred, but candidates with a strong golf background and the ability to lead, teach, recruit, and connect with student-athletes are encouraged to apply. Montana Tech Athletics is committed to providing an outstanding student-athlete experience while competing at a championship level in the Frontier Conference and NAIA. Duties: The Head Golf Coach is responsible for the leadership and operation of Montana Tech’s men’s and women’s golf programs, with primary emphasis on student-athlete instruction, coaching, development, and recruitment. Duties include planning and conducting practices, providing technical and strategic instruction, coaching during competition, evaluating and recruiting prospective student-athletes, and fostering a positive team culture consistent with Montana Tech Athletics and NAIA expectations. The position will work collaboratively with the Athletic Department, which will provide support for many administrative functions, including student-athlete eligibility and compliance, travel planning and arrangements, scheduling logistics, purchasing, and other operational responsibilities. This structure is intended to allow the Head Coach to focus primarily on coaching, recruiting, student-athlete development, and competitive success. Required Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree or an equivalent combination of education and relevant professional experience. Demonstrated knowledge of the game of golf, including fundamentals, technique, strategy, and player development. Experience coaching, teaching, instructing, or developing golfers. Ability to recruit, develop, motivate, and mentor student-athletes. Strong interpersonal and communication skills and the ability to build positive relationships with student-athletes, prospective student-athletes and their families, campus partners, alumni, and supporters. Commitment to student-athlete academic success, personal development, sportsmanship, and well-being. Ability to lead and foster a positive, accountable, and competitive team culture. Ability and willingness to travel and work evenings and weekends as required for practices, competitions, and recruiting. Valid driver’s license or ability to obtain one as required for team travel. Commitment to complying with Montana Tech, Frontier Conference, and NAIA rules, policies, and expectations. Preferred Qualifications: Previous experience coaching or instructing golf and demonstrated ability to recruit, develop, and build positive relationships with student-athletes. For full consideration application materials must be complete. Please include: Cover letter addressing qualifications, Resume Contact information for 3 professional references. Application Requirements For full consideration application materials must be complete. Any offer of employment is contingent upon a satisfactory criminal background check. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement Montana Tech is committed to providing a working and learning environment free from discrimination. As such, the University does not discriminate in the admission, access to or conduct of its educational programs and activities nor in its employment policies and practices on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, ethnicity, creed, service in the uniformed services (as defined in state and federal law), veteran status, gender, age, political beliefs, marital or family status, pregnancy, physical or mental disability, genetic information, gender identity, gender expression, or sexual orientation or preference. In support of the University's mission to be inclusive and diverse, applications from qualified minorities, women, veterans and persons with disabilities are highly encouraged. Montana Tech makes accommodation for any known disability that may interfere with an applicant's ability to compete in the hiring process or an employee's ability to perform the duties of the job. In compliance with the Montana Veteran's Employment Preference Act, Montana Tech provides preference in employment to veterans, disabled veterans, and certain eligible relatives of veterans. Employment Eligibility: All New Employees must be eligible and show employment eligibility verification by the first date of employment at Montana Tech as legally required (e.g., Form I-9). Montana Tech will require proof of authorization to work in the United States before final hiring. Due to the September 19, 2025 Presidential Proclamation and related guidance from USCIS and the Department of State, the University may be limited in its ability to offer H-1B sponsorship. At this time, we are unable to sponsor new H-1B visas that require payment of the additional fee introduced by the Proclamation. Veterans Employment Preference To claim veteran's preference please complete the employment (veteran's) preference form located on the employment page and email to humanresources@mtech.edu. You must include the job title of the position in which you are applying. Download Employment (Veteran's) Preference Form (PDF) Request an Accommodation To request an accommodation for the application or interview, please contact Cathy Isakson at 406-496-4380 or email cisakson@mtech.edu Why Work at Tech? Help meet the changing needs of society by providing a transformative student experience by helping develop leaders for tomorrow by advancing science, engineering and technology. Benefits Package In addition, Montana Tech offers an attractive benefits package* which includes: Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance with low deductibles and comprehensive coverage. Generous employer contribution toward monthly health care benefits worth $6.08 per hour. 5.9% retirement employer contribution for eligible employees 11 Holidays per year 3 weeks of Annual Leave to start Generous sick leave policy that can be used for sick children, doctor and dentist appointments as well as bereavement. 6 credits of coursework free per year (fees not included) Life and Disability Insurance Reduced tuition for dependents after 4 months of employment for eligible employees Employee Assistance and a Wellness Program Optional Retirement Plan for eligible employees Possible remote work days with supervisor approval and eligible positions. *Benefits are dependent on position type and terms and conditions of eligibility. About Montana Tech Montana Technological University, Butte Montana, is nestled in the Heart of the Rocky Mountains along the Continental Divide, where I-15 and I-90 intersect. We are home to the largest National Historic District in the country. Montana Tech is a special focus institution with a reputation for excellence and value. Montana Tech is ranked #1 in the nation by CollegeNET. Share Apply Apply for this position Required * First Name * Last Name * Email Address * Phone * Address * Resume * We've received your resume. Click here to update it. Attach resume or Paste resume Attach resume as .pdf, .doc, .docx, .odt, .txt, or .rtf (limit 5MB) or Paste resume Paste your resume here or Attach resume file Cover Letter * Have you ever been convicted of a felony? * No answer No Yes If “Yes”, you have been convicted of a felony, please explain the circumstances around the conviction: * References: Please enter names and contact information: * Do you have a Bachelor’s degree or an equivalent combination o